## FORBIDDEN PATTERNS

### Packages — never install these
framer-motion, mongoose (in web/), express, @tanstack/react-query,
@tanstack/react-virtual, react-router-dom, redux, zustand, jotai,
recoil, mobx, valtio, xstate, moment, date-fns, dayjs, luxon,
styled-components, @emotion/styled, react-youtube, react-player,
slugify (npm), bullmq, redis, web-push, react-modal, react-spring,
auto-animate, @vercel/og, @sentry/react, @sentry/nextjs

### Patterns — never write these
- Modal-driven CRUD forms (admin uses route-level pages)
- TanStack Query on any read path
- Context providers above the card list that cause grid re-renders
  on bookmark toggle, stream switch, or tag filter change
- useEffect chains that sync URL params into useState or context
- rehype-raw plugin (XSS risk)
- Bookmark state in a context provider — it is local to each card
- Full grid remount on filter change — filters drive RSC via URL
- service role key outside lib/supabase/admin.ts
- is_published anywhere in application TypeScript

### Legacy patterns from Project-Phoenix — do not port
- ArticleModal / ArticleDrawer — replaced by the canonical /nuggets/[id]/[slug] route; only route-driven intercepted sheet shells are allowed
- FilterStateContext — replaced by nuqs URL state
- useInfiniteArticles hook — replaced by fetch + useTransition
- BookmarkCollection / CollectionSelector — replaced by flat /bookmarks
- NewsCard grid/feed/masonry variants — single dense grid only
- openArticle / expanded URL sync pattern — replaced by next/link to the canonical route; never reintroduce query-param modal state

